# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER COMMIT: the legacy WordPress export.
# It contains plaintext customer license keys and Office 365 / Adobe account
# passwords inside wp_comments (order notes), plus a 346 MB site tarball.
# Treat it as a secret asset. See docs/plan.html section 02.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Old Website/
*.sql
*.sql.gz
*.tar.gz
*.wpress

# ...but not the project's own SQL. The *.sql rule above is aimed at the legacy
# database dump, and it was quietly taking the schema's entire history with it:
# every Prisma migration and the role bootstrap that docker-compose mounts into
# a fresh Postgres. A clone of this repo could not build its own database.
!packages/db/prisma/migrations/**/*.sql
!packages/db/prisma/init/*.sql

# Extracted legacy uploads and the media import's processed output. Same rule
# as Old Website/ — it comes out of the backup, so it never goes in the repo.
.cache/

# One-off scratch scripts. These get written next to a package so its own
# dependencies resolve, and then they get committed by accident.
code.mjs
check.mts

# secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# deps & build
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
dist/
build/
.next/
out/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# prisma generated client
packages/db/generated/

# Generated by `pnpm --filter @da/api openapi` and published by CI as an
# artefact. Not committed: a checked-in copy is one nobody regenerates.
apps/api/openapi.json

# test & tooling output
coverage/
.nyc_output/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.lighthouseci/

# editors & os
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
# ...except the governance logs, which are the project's audit trail.
!project-management/logs/*.log

# Compiler output emitted beside the source by a stray `tsc` without -p.
# Builds go to dist/; a map in src/ is always an accident.
packages/*/src/**/*.map

# Agent OS hook metrics (tool-call counts, guard decisions). Local only.
.claude/metrics/
# Canonical-state lock, held while a pm command writes.
agent-os/state/*.lock

# Design handoff packages (~227 MB of PNG/WebP). Reviewed in docs/ui-kit-review.md;
# only the editable source and artwork assets get imported, never the full export.
docs/Digital_Activation_UI_Kit_AR_EN/
docs/Digital_Activation_Real_Product_Banners_AR_EN_v2/
